-# app/views/keyserver/shared/_demographic_matrix.html.haml

%section
  %h2 Demographic Usage
  Consider these scenarios: 
  %ul
    %li 
      %strong{ style: "font-weight: 700 !important;" } Power Users
      are  revealed by a high number of uses and a low number of unique patrons.
      This is a small, highly dedicated core audience.
    %li
      %strong{ style: "font-weight: 700 !important;" } Low Retention
      is revealed by a low number of uses and a high number of unique patrons.
      This highlights a group that tries the service but doesn't return.
    %li 
      %strong{ style: "font-weight: 700 !important;" } Maximum Impact
      is revealed by a high number of uses and a high number of unique patrons.
      This shows the most successful, broadly adopted segment.

  %h3 Absolute Usage
  - total_users = @raw_demo_matrix.values.sum { |nested_hash| nested_hash.values.sum { |info| info[:value] } }
  - if total_users == 0
    %p No data available for this time period
  - else
    %table{style: "width: 100%; margin: 0 auto;"}
      %thead
        %tr
          %th Patron Type / Affiliation
          - @user_groups.each do |user_group|
            %th{style: "width: 100px;"}= user_group
      %tbody
        - @affiliations.each do |school| 
          %tr
            %td.row-header
              %strong= school
            - @user_groups.each do |user_group|
              = shaded_cell_tag(@raw_demo_matrix.dig(user_group, school))
    %br
  %br
  %h3 Unique Patron Usage
  - if total_users == 0
    %p No data available for this time period
  - else
    %table{style: "width: 100%; margin: 0 auto;"}
      %thead
        %tr
          %th Patron Type / Affiliation
          - @user_groups.each do |user_group|
            %th{style: "width: 100px;"}= user_group
      %tbody
        - @affiliations.each do |school| 
          %tr
            %td.row-header
              %strong= school
            - @user_groups.each do |user_group|
              = shaded_cell_tag(@distinct_demo_matrix.dig(user_group, school))
    %br
